05:01 But you, Beit-Lechem Efratah, which are little to be among the thousands of Yehudah, out of you shall one come forth to me that is to be ruler in Yisra'el; whose goings forth are from of old, from everlasting.
05:02 Therefore will he give them up, until the time that she who travails has brought forth: then the residue of his brothers shall return to the children of Yisra'el.
05:03 He shall stand, and shall feed his flock in the strength of HaSHEM, in the majesty of the name of HaSHEM his G-D: and they shall abide; for now shall he be great to the ends of the earth.
05:04 This man shall be our shalom. When the Ashshur shall come into our land, and when he shall tread in our palaces, then shall we raise against him seven shepherds, and eight principal men.
05:05 They shall waste the land of Ashshur with the sword, and the land of Nimrod in the entrances of it: and he shall deliver us from the Ashshur, when he comes into our land, and when he treads within our border.
05:06 The remnant of Ya`akov shall be in the midst of many peoples as dew from HaSHEM, as showers on the grass, that don't wait for man, nor wait for the sons of men.
05:07 The remnant of Ya`akov shall be among the nations, in the midst of many peoples, as a lion among the animals of the forest, as a young lion among the flocks of sheep; who, if he go through, treads down and tears in pieces, and there is none to deliver.
05:08 Let your hand be lifted up above your adversaries, and let all your enemies be cut off.
05:09 It shall happen in that day, says HaSHEM, that I will cut off your horses out of the midst of you, and will destroy your chariots:
05:10 and I will cut off the cities of your land, and will throw down all your strongholds.
05:11 I will cut off witchcraft out of your hand; and you shall have no more soothsayers:
05:12 and I will cut off your engraved images and your pillars out of the midst of you; and you shall no more worship the work of your hands;
05:13 and I will pluck up your Asherim out of the midst of you; and I will destroy your cities.
05:14 I will execute vengeance in anger and wrath on the nations which didn't listen.  
06:01 Hear you now what HaSHEM says: Arise, contend you before the mountains, and let the hills hear your voice.
06:02 Hear, you mountains, HaSHEM's controversy, and you enduring foundations of the earth; for HaSHEM has a controversy with his people, and he will contend with Yisra'el.
06:03 My people, what have I done to you? and in which have I wearied you? testify against me.
06:04 For I brought you up out of the land of Mitzrayim, and redeemed you out of the house of bondage; and I sent before you Moshe, Aharon, and Miryam.
06:05 My people, remember now what Balak king of Mo'av devised, and what Bil`am the son of Be'or answered him; remember from Shittim to Gilgal, that you may know the righteous acts of HaSHEM.
06:06 Wherewith shall I come before HaSHEM, and bow myself before the high G-D? shall I come before him with burnt offerings, with calves a year old?
06:07 will HaSHEM be pleased with thousands of rams, or with ten thousands of rivers of oil? shall I give my firstborn for my disobedience, the fruit of my body for the sin of my soul?
06:08 He has showed you, man, what is good; and what does HaSHEM require of you, but to do justly, and to love kindness, and to walk humbly with your G-D?
06:09 The voice of HaSHEM cries to the city, and the man of wisdom will see your name: hear you the rod, and who has appointed it.
06:10 Are there yet treasures of wickedness in the house of the wicked, and a scant measure that is abominable?
06:11 Shall I be pure with wicked balances, and with a bag of deceitful weights?
06:12 For the rich men of it are full of violence, and the inhabitants of it have spoken lies, and their tongue is deceitful in their mouth.
06:13 Therefore I also have struck you with a grievous wound; I have made you desolate because of your sins.
06:14 You shall eat, but not be satisfied; and your humiliation shall be in the midst of you: and you shall put away, but shall not save; and that which you save will I give up to the sword.
06:15 You shall sow, but shall not reap; you shall tread the olives, but shall not anoint you with oil; and the vintage, but shall not drink the wine.
06:16 For the statutes of `Omri are kept, and all the works of the house of Ach'av, and you walk in their counsels; that I may make you a desolation, and the inhabitants of it a hissing: and you shall bear the reproach of my people.  
07:01 Woe is me! for I am as when they have gathered the summer fruits, as the grape gleanings of the vintage: there is no cluster to eat; my soul desires the first-ripe fig.
07:02 The godly man is perished out of the earth, and there is none upright among men: they all lie in wait for blood; they hunt every man his brother with a net.
07:03 Their hands are on that which is evil to do it diligently; the prince asks, and the judge is ready for a reward; and the great man, he utters the evil desire of his soul: thus they weave it together.
07:04 The best of them is as a brier; the most upright is worse than a thorn hedge: the day of your watchmen, even your visitation, is come; now shall be their perplexity.
07:05 Don't you trust in a neighbor; don't you put confidence in a friend; keep the doors of your mouth from her who lies in your bosom.
07:06 For the son dishonors the father, the daughter rises up against her mother, the daughter-in-law against her mother-in-law; a man's enemies are the men of his own house.
07:07 But as for me, I will look to HaSHEM; I will wait for the G-D of my salvation: my G-D will hear me.
07:08 Don't rejoice against me, my enemy: when I fall, I shall arise; when I sit in darkness, HaSHEM will be a light to me.
07:09 I will bear the indignation of HaSHEM, because I have sinned against him, until he plead my cause, and execute judgment for me: he will bring me forth to the light, and I shall see his righteousness.
07:10 Then my enemy shall see it, and shame shall cover her who said to me, Where is HaSHEM your G-D? My eyes shall see my desire on her; now shall she be trodden down as the mire of the streets.
07:11 A day for building your walls! in that day shall the decree be far removed.
07:12 In that day shall they come to you from Ashshur and the cities of Mitzrayim, and from Mitzrayim even to the River, and from sea to sea, and from mountain to mountain.
07:13 Yet shall the land be desolate because of those who dwell therein, for the fruit of their doings.
07:14 Feed your people with your rod, the flock of your heritage, which dwell solitarily, in the forest in the midst of Karmel: let them feed in Bashan and Gil`ad, as in the days of old.
07:15 As in the days of your coming forth out of the land of Mitzrayim will I show to them marvelous things.
07:16 The nations shall see and be ashamed of all their might; they shall lay their hand on their mouth; their ears shall be deaf.
07:17 They shall lick the dust like a serpent; like crawling things of the earth they shall come trembling out of their close places; they shall come with fear to HaSHEM our G-D, and shall be afraid because of you.
07:18 Who is a G-D like you, that pardons iniquity, and passes over the disobedience of the remnant of his heritage? he doesn't retain his anger forever, because he delights in lovingkindness.
07:19 He will again have compassion on us; he will tread our iniquities under foot; and you will cast all their sins into the depths of the sea.
07:20 You will perform the truth to Ya`akov, and the lovingkindness to Avraham, which you have sworn to our fathers from the days of old.  
